      "dcterms:title": "Fiber Functors of Equivariantizations of Finite Tensor Categories",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "CÉSAR GALINDO, CLAUDIA GALLEGO",
        "MORALES, YIBY"
      ],
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.10525",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Let G be a finite group acting on a finite tensor category C. We classify fiber functors on the equivariantization CG in terms of equivariant exact module categories over C, indexed by subgroups of G. The data are a subgroup H ⊆G and an H-equivariant C-module category M whose underlying C-module category is indecomposable, exact, and semisimple; they give a fiber functor precisely when H acts transitively on the simple objects of M and the stabilizer cocycle of one, hence every, simple object is non-degenerate. Through Tannaka–Krein reconstruction this describes realizations of CG as the representation category of a finite-dimensional Hopf algebra, with no semisimplicity hypothesis on C. As applications, for odd primes p we determine the fiber functors on Rep(Hp), where Hp denotes Nikshych’s semisimple Hopf algebra of dimension 4p2 [Nik08]: there is one equivalence class if p ≡3 (mod 4) and two if p ≡1 (mod 4). We also use the classification for gaugings to determine which non-pointed entries in the small-dimensional list of [GN25] are representation categories of semisimple factorizable Hopf algebras.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2607.10525v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2607.10525v1"
    }
  ]
}
